# structgen arguments for sdk/ts/gen/game_layout.<build>.ts, and for the
# SG_LAYOUT_HASH c/Makefile bakes into each wasm module (wasm_layout_hash).
# Read by tools/structgen/gen.sh and c/Makefile, both with --cwd c/ and the
# build's own flags, so the module and the wasm hash come from ONE argument list.
# Lines starting with # are dropped; everything else is split on whitespace.
#
# The resident Game prefix the TS marshal reads and writes.
--header game.h --root Game
--fields Game=status,num_players,power_suit,first_attacker,defender,num_battles,deck_count,discard_pile_length,has_flipped,deterministic_deck,flipped,deck,table_battles,players,elimination_order,num_eliminated,good_players_mask,has_good_timestamp
--fields Player=status,hand_count,awaiting_attack,strategy_key,hand
--const GAME_STATUS_ --const PLAYER_STATUS_
#
# The C Table (c/src/table.h): what the server reads back from bots.wasm - the
# loaded roster, a commit's spans and scalars, a decoded action request, the
# finish order and rating changes - and the result codes it maps. Part of the
# same hash, so a module and these readers cannot disagree about any of it.
--header table.h --root Roster --root TableCommit --root TableRequest --root TableElo
--const TABLE_ --const ENGINE_REJECT_ --const GAME_INVALID_ --const ROSTER_E_
#
# The web client's slot (client_table.h): hashed here so a stale
# view_layout.bots.ts (specs/view_layout.args) is a load-time error too.
--header client_table.h --root TableView --root PushEvent
#
# The bot cycle the table drives (bot_drive.h): what a server logs of it.
--header bot_drive.h --root BotDriveOut
--fields LegalMove=type,n_cards,cards,attack_cards
--const BOT_STOP_ --const BOT_PACE_ --const MOVE_
#
# Test fixtures (e2e/helpers/table_fixture.ts): card notation refusals and suit
# numbers (card.h), and the durable roster's length a sealed row carries.
--const CARD_PARSE_E_ --const SUIT_ --const ROSTER_BYTES
